MMC99 @MMC99_VERSION@ - a C99 compiler for Windows and Linux programs

Unzip this folder anywhere. Nothing else needs to be installed.

Compile and run a program:

    bin\MMC99.exe hello.c -o hello.exe
    hello.exe

Build the same program for Linux (run it on Linux, or in WSL):

    bin\MMC99.exe --target=x86_64-pc-linux-gnu hello.c -o hello

A Linux program needs glibc 2.34 or newer (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12 and later).

To type MMC99 from any folder, add this folder's bin to PATH.
"MMC99 --help" lists every option.

MMC99 compiles all of C99 and uses each system's own C library: MinGW-w64's
on Windows, glibc on Linux, with all of their headers, windows.h included.
A header that needs an extension MMC99 does not support fails with an error
message; MMC99 never builds a wrong program from it.

CONFORMANCE.md documents every choice C99 leaves to the compiler, and every
extension. SOURCES.txt says where every file comes from; licenses holds their
licenses.
